WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.520
Before we begin, let me grace you with some
breaking news regarding checkpoints.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.269
So for a while, we've had this screenshot..of
two pot guys standing around a sliver of gold

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:16.700
- but now, we know what that sliver of gold
represents. Recently, the following description

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.810
was captioned alongside this image in the
Japanese gaming magazine "Famitsu". It reads:

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:28.039
"Graces will act in a similar manner to Dark
Souls bonfires, acting as a checkpoint/base

00:00:28.039 --> 00:00:30.109
for the player".

00:00:30.109 --> 00:00:39.040
So there you go! The word "base" is interesting..and
I really hope these places act as more of

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.660
a mobile camp, in some way.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:47.660
But what are "Graces", from a lore point of
view?. Well, according to a recent tweet from

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:53.460
the Elden Ring twitter, before the shattering,
the Lands Between basked in the pure light

00:00:53.460 --> 00:01:00.150
of the Greater Will. Slivers of its blessing
yet remain in hidden pockets, where lost graces

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.890
wait to be found.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:06.829
So these are places where the grace of the
Greater Will remains..and you can expect to

00:01:06.829 --> 00:01:09.380
set up camp around these places, along your
journey. (Special thanks to Mordecai of Elden

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.380
Ring News for first reporting on this).

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.380
1

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.200
Now, back to the trailer. So some people are
going into Elden Ring completely blind..and

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.950
some are only going to watch the trailer once.
Me? Well I've watched it so many times I'm

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:26.149
single-handedly responsible for Elden Ring
being the most viewed trailer over the E3

00:01:26.149 --> 00:01:33.119
period. I've also watched it frame by frame,
and you might be surprised at some of the

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:39.350
things I've found. Here are all its secrets..big,
and small.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:46.679
First, this gauntlet is the same one worn
by the "Tarnished" character who features

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:51.649
prominently in this trailer. He's featured
so heavily here that you'd think he might

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:57.430
be a sort of cover character for the game,
but that role is apparently going to this

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.929
knight, instead.

00:01:58.929 --> 00:02:03.749
At the very least, it might actually be an
option to start with this armour set. There

00:02:03.749 --> 00:02:10.360
are 10 starting classes to choose from, apparently..and
this this cutscene strikes me in a similar

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:16.170
way to Sekiro's opening, where the maiden
approaches our character, who is left for

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.170
dead.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:22.820
You can actually see her riding in on Yakul
at the start. If I had to guess, she's passing

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.290
this mount over to us here.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:30.310
She has a faded scar, or birthmark, and a
ring, on her right hand.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:36.670
She pulls this ring off, and passes it to
us. Now, her lips aren't moving in sync with

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:40.710
this dialogue..but it does seem appropriate
for what's going on.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:44.500
"The Tarnished will rise, guided by grace
once lost"

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.500
2

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:52.220
I wouldn't be surprised if that line was quite
literal, with the light from the tree guiding

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:56.550
you to points of interest on the map. Powerful
items maybe, or checkpoints.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:03.510
Speaking of points of interest, here are some.
A cliffside gate...ruins in the bottom right..small

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:10.580
buildings here, and here..and a swamp in the
bottom left. These shallow waters seem to

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:16.360
be found in the canyons cutting through the
map..which may or may not have been caused

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.640
by some sort of cataclsysm?

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:24.210
In previous leaks, that bridge in the distance
was unbroken..but now, debris from the bridge

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:30.120
appears to be scattered across the entire
landscape, suggesting some thing tore through

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.650
this area. That castle on the left appears
to be the main Legacy dungeon..and it too

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.930
is pretty scarred.

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:43.440
It's a beautifully ruined scene, made better
when you notice the golden specs flying through

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:49.840
the air aren't embers like they would be in
Dark Souls..they're leaves, from the tree.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:50.970
Perhaps its dying?

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:51.970
3

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:58.340
We see more of the shallows in this next scene.
Here, homes and spires seem to have sunk into

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.440
the earth, more proof that ruin has come to
the Lands Between.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.570
In the distance we see a familiar tower, but
it's hard to say which one..because there

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:03.570
were multiples of these in the previous scene.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:08.090
Here, birds fly overhead..and it seems to
be a misty morning, which makes me wonder

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:13.790
if the mist comes with the time of day, or
with the area.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:20.400
The same goes for the golden leaves, which
are not falling in this morning scene, despite

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.280
the tree being quite close.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.280
4

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:29.479
In the next scene, we're treated to yet another
skybox, our eyes drawn then to a sort of volcano

00:04:29.479 --> 00:04:36.050
in the distance. I suggest it's a volcano..because
this rocky texture is seen again in this dragon

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:40.879
scene, where magma sits on the ground. (/u/tripledoble)

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:47.340
As your eyes travel down, we realise that
this autumnal scene has a different atmospheric

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:56.100
affect, with blue white light floating upwards.
This ethereal atmosphere helps to explain

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:06.440
the giant phantom flagpole, which itself has
hints of interlocking rings upon it.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:12.849
On the ground are two encampments, filled
with what surely are enemies. Like the phantom

00:05:12.849 --> 00:05:17.319
flagpole, one tent also features a design
with interlocking rings, and their banner

00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:24.569
features a giant tree, suggesting an affiliation
with the Erdtree, and the Elden Ring that

00:05:24.569 --> 00:05:25.759
is at its source.

00:05:25.759 --> 00:05:26.759
5

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:30.580
Considering all this symbolism, it's probably
no coincidence that these scenes are accompanied

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:36.409
by the line "The Golden Order is broken to
its core", and this second shot really drives

00:05:36.409 --> 00:05:42.389
that point home. Here, we see yet another
crest of interlocking rings...and this one

00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:48.689
looks a lot like the Elden Ring logo, except
with even more circles, and a mess of tendrils

00:05:48.689 --> 00:05:50.790
running down from it.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:55.319
Below, a person kneels, surrounded by three
wolves.

00:05:55.319 --> 00:06:02.360
The appearance of beasts here maybe no coincidence..for
this is actually where we fight the beast

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:06.599
clad in black and gold armour, later in the
trailer.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:15.000
You can tell, because that arena also features
these same pillars, filled with skeletal remains.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:20.150
Filling your architecture with corpses is
pretty dark for a group called the Golden

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:26.180
Order, though there is plentiful evidence
of this sort of immurement within history,

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:27.500
and folklore.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.069
Lastly, we hear crow noises..but in the background,
we actually see dragons flying by. Apparently,

00:06:31.069 --> 00:06:35.639
the Golden Order isn't the only thing broken..so
is this flying animation. Preorder cancelled.

00:06:35.639 --> 00:06:36.639
6

00:06:36.639 --> 00:06:41.569
Next we see a very literal bonfire, surrounded
by people frozen in place, for some reason.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:47.681
There are also what look like red flowers
under these trees - things like this are seen

00:06:47.681 --> 00:06:54.599
throughout the trailer..and the way they glow
makes me wonder if these are gather-able resources.

00:06:54.599 --> 00:06:59.400
It's raining in this scene, another obvious
weather effect to be added to the list..

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.400
7

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:09.680
..and another time of day to add to the list,
might be this sunset. I wonder if we literally

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:30.650
get to watch the sun go through the sky, and
how fast the days will go?

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:36.939
The character has a horn by their waist, which
we see throughout the trailer. Assuming it's

00:07:36.939 --> 00:07:40.449
a part of your equipment, I wonder what it
does..

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:41.449
8

00:07:41.449 --> 00:07:46.059
It's definitely not used to call for Yakul.
Instead, that's done with a simple whistle

00:07:46.059 --> 00:07:48.509
that sounds a lot like the one from Sekiro.

00:07:48.509 --> 00:07:53.900
Here, the character is actually jumping over
graves sticking out oddly from the wall, which

00:07:53.900 --> 00:08:02.020
are better seen in this screenshot. Birds
are perched around the place in this screenshot,

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:03.999
as well.

00:08:03.999 --> 00:08:10.619
If you pause here, you can see that Yakul
actually has rings of gold on his horns, something

00:08:10.619 --> 00:08:18.180
seen even more clearly in this screenshot.
Maybe he has some lost grace of his own.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:24.520
Finally, we clearly see a standard longsword
in this shot. Start that weapon tally.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.680
9

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:31.050
As the camera pans out, you can start to piece
together the geography. For example, we approach

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:37.300
this castle and foggy valley from the front
here..but this next scene shows us the castle

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:43.050
and valley from the side, meaning we must
have traveled along this rocky cliff face

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.769
on the right in the previous scene.

00:08:44.769 --> 00:08:49.360
There's actually a tiny enemy here who is
having trouble loading in..

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:51.350
There's a small house here..

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:54.930
and many other buildings shrouded by fog further
on.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:09:00.820
Glowing lights can be seen below the bridge..one
blue, one gold..perhaps they're items, or

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:07.600
a grace? If I wanted to get down there, could
I jump off this cliff, and double jump on

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.920
Yakul before I hit the ground?

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:10.920
10

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.880
What follows is the scene with the walking
island. Previously, I speculated that you

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:23.040
might have to use surrounding geography to
jump on top of it at the right moment..but

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:29.050
reddit user /u/Kid_darkness93 seems to have
noticed a jump pad nearby, which looks like

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.970
a very likely alternative.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:36.639
I'm sure there are multiple ways up there..and
judging by the moss growing on the legs, I'd

00:09:36.639 --> 00:09:43.110
bet that this island only ever roams this
swampy area. It is going VERY slowly though...so

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.009
it might take a while to catch it in the right
spot.

00:09:46.009 --> 00:09:47.009
11

00:09:47.009 --> 00:09:51.410
In this mounted encounter, the enemy has a
curved greatsword wrapped in cloth, seen later

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:53.180
on in this clip.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:58.709
In regards to the guarded caravan, well I
always thought it looks like a coffin of some

00:09:58.709 --> 00:10:05.589
kind..and my favourite theory is that it's
transporting body parts, since that seems

00:10:05.589 --> 00:10:07.560
to be the trade of this area..

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.560
12

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:14.190
Here, we see a ton of hanging limbs, hooked
so crudely that they're spilling blood onto

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:20.949
the floor and dining tables below. Many of
these arms are conjoined, or double-ended,

00:10:20.949 --> 00:10:23.740
suggesting experimentation.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:28.710
Arms really are a big theme of this area..and
on both sides of the painting, you can make

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:36.390
out the lion emblem on these banners..the
same emblem that shows up on this castle,

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:40.490
on these soldiers, and on this big bosses
axe.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:50.610
The painting itself is very difficult to make
out - but there's a human figure there - with

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:54.480
some sort of fur pelt or animal draped over
his shoulders.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:58.720
Moving on, the flattened face to follow has
something that looks like a third eye on its

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.370
forehead, and the roots underneath almost
look like tentacles.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:11.389
Speaking of which, the statues to follow,
also in a cave, ALSO seem to have tentacles

00:11:11.389 --> 00:11:12.620
inside their robes.

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:13.620
13

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:18.829
And what about these pot guys? Do you think
they're hostile, or friendly? After years

00:11:18.829 --> 00:11:25.300
of smashing pots, is it finally time for pots
to smash us? Personally, I'd hope they're

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:31.820
friendly..you do see them around a grace checkpoint,
after all. What will be truly terrifying is

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:39.260
if they're friendly AND drop good loot, like
crystal lizards. Their arms do seem like they're

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:43.800
made of a similar texture..no..don't make
me do it..

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.730
As you continue underground, you might have
noticed that a grill is missing, suggesting

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.579
you can go further below.

00:11:51.579 --> 00:11:55.089
Then we come across another many-armed enemy.
This one is exuding green fumes, made of skull

00:11:55.089 --> 00:11:56.089
textures.

00:11:56.089 --> 00:12:00.279
Interestingly, he's wearing a crown..just
like the other many-armed character we see

00:12:00.279 --> 00:12:06.720
later in the trailer. That's an interesting
trend - maybe this kingdom's habit of experimentation

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.700
with limbs goes back quite a ways.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.700
14

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.279
Finally leaving the underground, we enter
the castle, which has diagonal gashes here,

00:12:13.279 --> 00:12:14.279
and further on.

00:12:14.279 --> 00:12:19.199
This boss blocks our progession, and a golden
fog gate appears behind him, blocking our

00:12:19.199 --> 00:12:20.199
progression.

00:12:20.199 --> 00:12:26.060
His robes, and magic weapons, mark him as
a sort of sorcerer. Design wise, he looks

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:34.080
a lot like the Ghru of Dark Souls 3, who have
similar twisting horns on their head. He also

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:37.800
has these same horns on the end of an enormous
tail.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:42.379
At first, it looks like these horns are ALL
there is making up his head..but you can actually

00:12:42.379 --> 00:12:44.570
see his face hidden below.

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:49.670
Interestingly, he also has a similar mess
of grey hair, like we do.

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:58.149
During the fight, you can see a sort of obelisk
with a blue light - the same sort seen later

00:12:58.149 --> 00:13:04.529
in the trailer, when the character summons
help. These summons also have a similar blue

00:13:04.529 --> 00:13:11.970
light - so I bet these stones mark the areas
you can summon at. Another summon is seen

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:21.120
in this area - a spirit bird, which..has prosthetic
legs? I'm so intrigued by this summon..it

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:27.589
seems like there's so much variety here.

00:13:27.589 --> 00:13:31.720
When the boss knocks us back, we get a good
view of our characters longsword, which is

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:39.399
imbued with a blue tint around the hilt, marking
it as a sort of magic weapon. The magic effect

00:13:39.399 --> 00:13:44.990
also appears around the weapon, marking it
as a sort of weapon art..and I wonder - can

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:50.660
magic weapon arts only be applied to magic
class weapons, like this longsword?

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:51.660
15

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:56.430
In the tunnel, there are some very brightly
glowing flowers that I bet we can loot..

00:13:56.430 --> 00:14:03.110
Followed by some enemies, one of which has
a conical hat, or helmet.

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.110
16

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.360
I love the weapon and armour of the character
in this scene.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:14.540
The enemy here has the lion crest on their
armour, and is also wearing a mask as a part

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.500
of their helmet, which we'll talk about later.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:25.589
They actually change the enemy during this
cut, and a golden glow heads towards our character

00:14:25.589 --> 00:14:32.230
after their death, giving us a hint at the
type of golden soul currency we can expect

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:33.510
to receive.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.510
17

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:39.530
It's similar to these golden leaves that fall
from the tree in this night time scene, which

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:46.290
look stunning against the blue sky.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:53.759
An enormous moon is visible, as are a couple
of crude tents. Now that graces are confirmed

00:14:53.759 --> 00:14:59.040
to be where our checkpoints lie, I'm less
convinced that we'll be able to set up camp

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:03.940
in the open world..but still kind of hopeful
that something like this might be in the game.

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:10.279
One cool thing to note is that the grass and
trees are blowing rapidly in the wind, which

00:15:10.279 --> 00:15:15.330
might mean they're reacting dynamically with
the weather, which is cool.

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:28.430
You can see the same sort of thing happening
to 

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:34.600
the trees in this stormy scene with the wolf
knight, who, as many have pointed out before

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:45.130
me, is an obvious Berserk reference. Sekiro
is a shinobi named wolf, Artorias was a wolf

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:51.290
knight..now we have this character, completing
the transformation. He even has a greatsword,

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.519
like Guts..I love the design.

00:15:53.519 --> 00:16:00.389
The way he's stepping off the edge of this
cliff in this animation means it must be the

00:16:00.389 --> 00:16:10.610
player character..and the long grey hair helps
to convince me of that. I'd imagine this is

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:16.209
something akin to the Dragon covenants of
Dark Souls, except we become a beast here

00:16:16.209 --> 00:16:22.889
instead? Perhaps this sort of transformation
is a path that tarnished can take..and if

00:16:22.889 --> 00:16:27.939
that's the case, can we turn into dragons
as well? This dragon has a spine of grey hair

00:16:27.939 --> 00:16:30.220
as well..just saying.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:31.220
18

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:36.810
This cube item is clearly the item we use
for summoning, and here it summons two helpers

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:42.740
which..both seem to be the same enemy model,
but equipped with slightly different gear?

00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:47.879
This one has a giant knife, and the other
has a sword..no wait it's a whip! aand you

00:16:47.879 --> 00:16:54.540
can see it snap back into being a sword again!
My best guess is that this is either a whip

00:16:54.540 --> 00:17:03.800
sword like the puzzling stone sword, or that
turning a sword into a whip is a type of weapon

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:09.250
art we can give it for extra range. Bit of
an odd one!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:13.579
This enemy has a cool greatsword, and our
character is doing the short bow dodge attack

00:17:13.579 --> 00:17:15.920
which will help make ranged play viable.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:16.920
19

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:22.939
Next, the dragon. It has four legs, four wings,
and a rocky texture..all things that would

00:17:22.939 --> 00:17:28.590
mark it as one of the greater Archdragons
of the Souls series. Another familiar souls

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:35.070
trope is summoning lightning - and since it
comes from the heavens, I bet the lightning

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:41.470
is a divine miracle here, similar to how it
is in Souls games, and Sekiro. If this Dragon

00:17:41.470 --> 00:17:45.799
is being blessed by the gods..man, that would
give Gwyn some serious conniptions.

00:17:45.799 --> 00:17:46.804
We, as the tarnished, are also being graced
again as well, remember..and even the dragon

00:17:46.804 --> 00:17:47.804
has a hint of grey hair running down its spine..so
maybe it's no different.

00:17:47.804 --> 00:17:52.850
As mentioned in another video, our character
is performing a double jump..not to avoid

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:58.789
the lightning per se, but instead to avoid
the ripple that goes along the ground from

00:17:58.789 --> 00:18:00.870
its point of contact.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:06.419
But look around the dragon this time..as mentioned
earlier, the rocks in the background match

00:18:06.419 --> 00:18:12.000
this smoking volcano, and we can even see
magma on the ground, underneath the flames.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:19.279
Look around some more..and here here, here,
here..piled up, and left discarded..are coffin

00:18:19.279 --> 00:18:26.190
carriages identical to the one the two giants
are hauling earlier in the trailer. For some

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:32.440
reason, it seems these coffin carriages are
being dumped in this volcano. Why?

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:37.700
This volcano also doesn't seem like the only
place we find the dragon. The next scene shows

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:45.090
it back in the open field, with no hint of
the rocky formation I just mentioned.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:52.750
Here we get our first side profile of the
sorcerer knight, holding an ornate staff sword

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:58.860
thing. They're fighting near the Erdtree,
but with a red sky. I wonder, is this burning

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:04.070
sky a special event, like the blood moon in
Breath of the Wild? Or is it a stage of the

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:08.830
game that changes the skybox, like we're used
to in previous games?

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:15.679
Finally, there's a strange corruption on the
ground here, that suits the red sky..

00:19:15.679 --> 00:19:16.679
20

00:19:16.679 --> 00:19:21.549
The next shot reveals a more feline beast
knight, also with long white hair, like us.

00:19:21.549 --> 00:19:22.549
His armour is black, trimmed with gold.

00:19:22.549 --> 00:19:25.380
In this scene, our character dual wields a
dagger and a short hatchet..two items that

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:31.990
would have the quickstep weapon art in Dark
Souls 3, and they seem to have it here as

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:32.990
well.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:39.840
The other way they avoid an attack is by jumping
this low sweep here, just like Sekiro would.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:40.840
21

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:46.279
As the trailer goes on, scenes pass faster..like
this one with the Valkyrie. Pausing the frame,

00:19:46.279 --> 00:19:54.220
we see two things - first, the clear corrosion
on her face..and second..a prosthetic..leg?

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:59.600
It's reflecting the light, showing a pattern..and
there's clearly a sort of bolt here keeping

00:19:59.600 --> 00:20:00.799
it in place. (ty to discussion with menaslg)

00:20:00.799 --> 00:20:06.120
As we get impaled - note that we're fighting
around the roots of a great tree. I wonder

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:08.070
if she's some sort of protector.

00:20:08.070 --> 00:20:09.070
22

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:14.890
In this scene, the bosses hand has six fingers..and
it's stroking the maw of a great, dead black

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:16.310
dragon.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:21.840
This is its nostril, and here is a giant horn.
It's actually the same head we see sewn onto

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:27.370
him at the end of the trailer...and the same
dragon seen briefly in the open world of the

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.760
leaked footage.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:34.690
So..does he attach the head halfway through
the fight? Is it a sort of phase 2 for him,

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:42.090
or is fighting him with it a sort of dynamic
event? He does do the roar cutscene in the

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:45.870
same place as the smash cutscene, after all..

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:52.309
In this cutscene, the tarnished draws his
sword slowly. Now..it's rare for a Souls game

00:20:52.309 --> 00:20:57.360
to have the player interact with their weapon
in a cutscene. The reason it's weird, is that

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:03.231
different characters have different weapons,
and drawing something like a greatsword, from

00:21:03.231 --> 00:21:10.910
the hip, wouldn't make sense. So..what's happening
here? Will this cutscene look the same regardless

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:16.820
of weapon? Did they come up with a unique
animation for each weapon type? Or is the

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:19.890
game pulling from a set of weapon drawing
animations? This one baffles me, honestly.

00:21:19.890 --> 00:21:24.690
On the bosses back, you can actually see Sekiro's
lost ar- just kidding. Though if I had to

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:29.549
guess, this would be the guy who took the
Valkyrie's arm, or at least is somewhat responsible

00:21:29.549 --> 00:21:35.559
for the arm theme throughout this area. He
also takes legs as well, you can see a couple

00:21:35.559 --> 00:21:42.760
hanging..and while his left leg seems to be
that of a giant..his right foot is a mess

00:21:42.760 --> 00:21:48.660
of toes. Eugh. There's some serious body horror
going on in this trailer.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:55.100
Finally, there's a lion crest on his main
axe, marking him as a lord of this castle,

00:21:55.100 --> 00:22:02.520
and region. According to the official twitter,
he's a Lord clinging to his ruined Legacy..the

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:06.059
ruler of a husk wrung dry by war.

00:22:06.059 --> 00:22:11.870
The word "Legacy" is capitalised..and legacy
dungeons were said to be the main levels within

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:22.340
each open world, each containing a demigod.
Therefore, he's the main boss of this area.

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:28.790
Man, the longer I hold off on making my story
video, the more scraps the Elden Ring twitter

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:31.650
bestows upon me. I'll just wait a liiitle
longer...

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:32.650
23

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:35.330
Here come the quickfire part of the trailer.
Here, a tarnished dual wields curved swords.

00:22:35.330 --> 00:22:40.880
Like in the previous scene, these are different
weapons..meaning we might be seeing a return

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:45.690
to the more dynamic way to dual wield multiple
weapons, like in Dark Souls 2.

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:49.330
The bramble knight also has a unique greatsword
that I'm sure he drops..

00:22:49.330 --> 00:22:53.770
and we're fighting him at night, under the
light of the Erdtree.

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:54.770
24

00:22:54.770 --> 00:23:01.290
Next, the dragon drive by. It's likely the
black horned dragon I mentioned earlier, though

00:23:01.290 --> 00:23:03.460
it's hard to say for sure.

00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:10.710
Here, the character carries a huge, two handed
spiked mace..and the same armour better seen

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:11.899
in this screenshot.

00:23:11.899 --> 00:23:12.899
25

00:23:12.899 --> 00:23:18.450
Next, lordvessel smough sends out a cascade
of flames, as he stands off against the sorcerer

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:22.700
knight, wielding the same wrapped greatsword
mentioned previously.

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:28.240
We also see a hint of his giant mace, which
I hope he drops..alongside that helmet.

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:29.240
26

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:35.610
The giant has one arm, meaning it's probably
going to show up somewhere else in the game

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:41.960
..and he has a flame smoldering deep within
his chest.

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:49.190
His weapon is a sort of axe staff, double
ended..and our weapon is a short blade with

00:23:49.190 --> 00:23:56.790
blue runes. It's the second time we've seen
a sorcery-themed sword with a blue tinged

00:23:56.790 --> 00:24:03.850
base..so I really do wonder if these are a
class of magic weapon now, or if magical properties

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:07.790
can be bestowed upon the weapon..at a blacksmith,
perhaps?

00:24:07.790 --> 00:24:08.790
27

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:14.809
Next, the castle..like Bloodborne crossed
with Irithyll. I love it. The gargoyle statues

00:24:14.809 --> 00:24:20.320
are seen again in this next indoors scene,
showing that they're the same place.

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:27.370
Here, our character wields a sorcery-halberd,
the enemies wield crossbows, rapiers..and

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:32.870
the main enemy has a simple sorcerer's staff.
His headpiece is already the focus of many

00:24:32.870 --> 00:24:34.820
burger king memes.

00:24:34.820 --> 00:24:39.530
Lastly, there's a bird in a small cage here
on the side here.

00:24:39.530 --> 00:24:40.530
28

00:24:40.530 --> 00:24:47.300
Speaking of animals, around the great stag,
visible even before it spawns, are many smaller,

00:24:47.300 --> 00:24:50.760
brighter ones wandering and grazing upon the
field.

00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:56.760
The masked player character in this shot is
the same as in this screenshot, except this

00:24:56.760 --> 00:24:59.799
time wielding claws, instead of a flail.

00:24:59.799 --> 00:25:00.799
29

00:25:00.799 --> 00:25:05.550
Speaking of masks..that's a bit of a theme
for the entire trailer. This character we

00:25:05.550 --> 00:25:12.289
kneel at has a mask..the woman beside the
giant knight has a mask..there's a giant masked

00:25:12.289 --> 00:25:19.029
cart, this enemy type has one too..masks.
They're a good way to prevent your animators

00:25:19.029 --> 00:25:26.740
from having to animate mouths in cutscenes,
so I bet that's why From are such fans of

00:25:26.740 --> 00:25:31.360
them here. That Demon's Souls remake is a
tough act to follow..

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:32.360
30

00:25:32.360 --> 00:25:37.610
In this next scene, we see that limbs aren't
the only body parts being repurposed..this

00:25:37.610 --> 00:25:44.429
guys helmet and upper body armour features
a ton of ears..all the better to hear those

00:25:44.429 --> 00:25:45.640
books with?

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:46.640
31

00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:53.059
Next, this hand has way too many fingers..and
gives me a real body horror chill, reminding

00:25:53.059 --> 00:26:00.360
me of those terrifying hands from the early
Zelda games.

00:26:00.360 --> 00:26:05.380
The middle finger has many rings, and one
ring has a giant purple gem.

00:26:05.380 --> 00:26:10.880
The player character here seems to be using
a black flame spray attack against the hand,

00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:12.600
to little effect.

00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:18.440
Behind the hand, we see a giant head..which
actually looks a lot like Void, from Berserk..

00:26:18.440 --> 00:26:24.720
And behind that, the Erdtree is still seen,
even though this is a snowy area. This tree

00:26:24.720 --> 00:26:29.120
must be pretty central to a lot of the open
worlds, I imagine.

00:26:29.120 --> 00:26:30.120
32

00:26:30.120 --> 00:26:34.929
This next scene happens fast, but it's a masked
carriage with three flamethrowers on each

00:26:34.929 --> 00:26:35.929
side.

00:26:35.929 --> 00:26:39.020
The character has a spear, and a greatshield.

00:26:39.020 --> 00:26:40.020
33

00:26:40.020 --> 00:26:46.059
The eye seems to be that of a cyclops, since
you can see the bridge of a nose here..and

00:26:46.059 --> 00:26:49.220
the 8 other marks are..more pupils?

00:26:49.220 --> 00:26:50.220
35

00:26:50.220 --> 00:26:55.559
The winged knight here is the same one we
saw standing next to the masked woman, with

00:26:55.559 --> 00:26:59.049
a flat helmet and horned greatshield.

00:26:59.049 --> 00:27:00.320
36

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:05.750
And finally, there's a giant tree on the tower
in the final cutscene, along with the same

00:27:05.750 --> 00:27:10.679
diagonal marks on the towers seen earlier.
I can't wait to learn about the history of

00:27:10.679 --> 00:27:12.480
this place.

00:27:12.480 --> 00:27:19.440
Let's end today with a snippet of an interview
featuring George R. R. Martin, where he finally

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:50.029
talks about 

00:27:50.029 --> 00:28:31.159
Elden Ring. Enjoy.

00:28:31.159 --> 00:28:56.980
Now, before you start saying Elden Ring is
a sequel to Dark Souls - no. I seriously doubt

00:28:56.980 --> 00:29:02.840
he accidentally revealed that it's a literal
sequel..he obviously just meant that it's

00:29:05.261 --> 00:29:07.971
But thank you for watching and supporting,
and enjoy watching the channel for the next

00:29:07.971 --> 00:29:08.201
few weeks, as we discuss this game to death.
I'll see you soon.

